WEBVTT

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.790
Gu's Dish

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.160
Nee-nee, it's morning. Get up.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:55.650
Oh, we're out of bread.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:01:01.580
All right, I'm gonna go for it 
today and cook our breakfast.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:04.120
Wow! You're gonna cook?

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.040
Take some spring vegetables,

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:09.240
add some salad oil, some salt and pepper...

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:11.980
Okay, eat up.

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:16.010
Mm, came out nice.

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:18.550
Gu's Dish

00:02:54.020 --> 00:03:01.030
<b>Episode 3</b>

00:02:54.020 --> 00:03:01.030
<b>We Got Motivated
During the Holiday Break</b>

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:58.260
So, Golden Week starts tomorrow, huh?

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:01.030
And yet we have tests. What a drag.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.910
You know, I was thinking...

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:06.280
They're a lot more fun when 
you can just watch them.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.540
Good luck.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.460
<i>Oh, shut up...</i>

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:13.290
Just sitting around makes me sleepy.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.520
Back row, gather the tests.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:19.970
I'll gather them!

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.970
Okay.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.580
All right, I'll just go grade these.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.810
You guys get ready for the next test.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:30.580
Senpai, did you do okay on the test?

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.580
I'm not sure.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.910
Japanese isn't my best subject.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:36.780
Natsumi, did you—

00:03:37.480 --> 00:03:39.120
Whoa. You look way too crushed.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.030
Not Japanese... Anything but Japanese...

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.800
You did that badly?

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.450
No, more like the questions were just evil!

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:52.410
What the heck do those "Explain what the
author was thinking here" questions mean?!

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.560
I'm not the author! 
How am I supposed to know?!

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.810
He might've been thinking, 
"I want some curry!"

00:03:58.810 --> 00:03:59.920
Yeah, but...

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.720
He was probably thinking, 
"Crap, my deadline's coming up!"

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:04.920
Right?!

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.180
Jeez, get over it.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.210
Ugh, why do I feel so frustrated?

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:10.470
I'm miserable!

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.190
You agree with me, don't you?

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:14.690
There were no questions 
like that on my test.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.880
Nattsun, Nattsun.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:25.320
Whoof.

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:32.780
Is that how you feel right now?

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:34.710
I have no idea what you mean!

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.890
But that's pretty much how I feel!

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:39.230
Japanese is nothing but "whoof!"

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.670
There, there.

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.370
Well, no point in getting down about it.

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:45.590
Natsumi-chan's tests begin here!

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:48.300
That just makes me more concerned...

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.060
What's our next test again?

00:04:50.270 --> 00:04:52.600
Uh... Science.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.790
Science is my throw-away subject.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:55.670
What's after that?

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:56.390
English.

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:58.020
No way, not English!

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.780
I'm Japanese.

00:04:59.780 --> 00:05:00.570
After that?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:01.970
That's the last one.

00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:10.010
Like I said, Natsumi-chan's tests end here.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:11.870
I guess they would.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.080
All right, I'll just give up gracefully.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.020
That was fast!

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:17.620
I'd rather give the questions 
than the answers.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.900
Hotarun, Hotarun. Say "pizza" ten times.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:22.630
Huh?

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:24.310
Um...

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:29.350
Pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza, 
pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza, pizza.

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.190
Okay, and what's this?

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.360
Your knee (hiza)?

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.950
Oh. I got it wrong.

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:37.730
You can't even give the right questions.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.480
Don't give up, just try studying.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.570
Easy to say...

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.740
Nii-chan, are you pretty good at English?

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:57.500
Hey, Nii-chan.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:00.960
Teach me English.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.290
C'mon. Purr, meow.

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:10.890
Yay!

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.260
He ticked me off, so I took his glasses!

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:14.900
You don't "yay" over that.

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:17.640
The break's almost over. What are you doing?

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:21.450
Nee-chan, I'll drop science, 
so give me an English question.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.510
What? I'd kind of like to study, myself.

00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:27.700
But if I get a bad grade,

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:30.660
you might get the blow-back from Mom's rage.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:38.080
So ask me something from here 
that's likely to be on the test.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.420
Sheesh...

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:44.590
Okay, translate this sentence to Japanese.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:45.840
Um...

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.100
Middle school students must have it rough.

00:06:47.020 --> 00:06:49.050
Huh? I don't know that last word.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.050
Yeah.

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:52.290
Hmm... Judging from the context...

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:55.570
"Bob said, 'Is this an elephant?'"

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.020
"No, it's a hippo."

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:59.780
Buzz! Wrong!

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:02.550
The last word isn't "hippo," it's "ant!"

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:04.020
Okay, next...

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.030
That's Bob's mistake, isn't it?

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.150
Huh?

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.010
Yep. It's Bob who's wrong.

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:11.360
See? Ren-chon and Hotarun say so, too.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.280
Huh? I didn't say anything yet...

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.700
Who would confuse an ant for an elephant?

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:18.500
That's just what the question says!

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.080
I can't deal with this. 
Forget about English.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.320
Teach me science.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:25.590
We only have about five 
minutes of break left.

00:07:26.140 --> 00:07:28.420
Better get moving, then! Bring it on!

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:32.380
What are the roots of dicotyledons like?

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:35.970
They don't move and they can be blunt, 
but they're nice at their roots!

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.340
<b>Taproot and lateral roots</b>

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:38.940
Are you stupid?

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:39.520
Huh?

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:42.900
But they make flowers bloom 
and give insects nectar.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.700
They're nice at their roots!

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:46.480
What's the problem? 
That's what popped into my head.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.740
Forget about that, 
just get to the next question!

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:52.200
Jeez, you're a pest...

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.470
Bacteria propagate by splitting 
their cells into two.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:56.660
What is this called?

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:58.080
Red Samba!

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:58.620
<b>Cell division</b>

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.950
What is this part of a microscope called?

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.670
Rolling Revolver!

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:02.660
<b>Objective lens</b>

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.750
What is the substance released 
when organic matter is burned?

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:05.700
<b>Carbon dioxide</b>

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:05.710
Smoke signals!

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.000
What should you do to smell ammonia?

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.210
Plead for your life!

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:09.200
<b>Waft it toward you with your hand</b>

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:11.230
What is this part of the nose called?

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:13.550
Whoa! That guy's got a 
toothbrush stuck up his nose!

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:13.540
<b>Olfactory bulb</b>

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.510
What is this organism called?

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.250
<b>Water flea</b>

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.260
Sasanaka-san's grandpa!

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:18.440
Okay! I can do this!

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:20.110
What makes you so confident?

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:21.640
You were just blurting out 
random stuff at the end!

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.650
Okay, everyone take your seats.

00:08:24.650 --> 00:08:28.150
Kazu-nee! I've gotta roll with 
this momentum! Gimme the test!

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.440
Wow, you sure are motivated.

00:08:30.780 --> 00:08:33.200
All right, then, let's get started.

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:37.160
Remember, you get a zero if 
you don't write your name.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.390
<i>Natsumi-chan can do this. 
Natsumi-chan can do this.</i>

00:08:39.390 --> 00:08:41.120
<i>Natsumi-chan can do this. 
Natsumi-chan can do this.</i>

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:44.460
Now... Begin.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:47.380
All right!

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.470
I can do this! Natsumi-chan, fight!

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:50.600
I can do it! I can do it!

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:52.810
Oh! This is one of the questions I just had!

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:54.810
The answer is "the Sasanaka 
family's grandpa"!

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:55.800
<i>Oh, shut up...</i>

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.960
Hey, I had this one before, too!

00:08:57.960 --> 00:08:59.410
Oh! And this one!

00:08:59.410 --> 00:09:02.100
Oh, man! Natsumi-chan 
might really be a genius!

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:07.730
Okay, I'm going to return today's tests.

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:11.690
Miyauchi Renge

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:11.690
Very Good Job

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:11.690
If you have any questions about 
your grade, bring it up.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.320
I didn't do as well as I thought...

00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:22.290
There's something weird about mine.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:24.500
Hm? Bring it up.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:26.660
Isn't this wrong?

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:28.000
Where?

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.250
This, right here.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:33.310
I wrote my name, but I still got a zero.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:38.470
Oh, right. This is because...

00:09:40.550 --> 00:09:43.290
...you got every question wrong.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:57.690
Whoof.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:05.570
So, Golden Week starts tomorrow,

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:08.710
but your tests weren't so great overall,

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:11.150
so I'm assigning homework.

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.800
Aww...

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:18.500
Yeah, this really is a lot more 
fun when you can just watch!

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:25.600
We sure got a lot of homework.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:28.480
All because Natsumi got a zero.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:37.130
There's...

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.690
Don't be hasty!

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:40.450
Huh? What?! Nee-chan, let go!

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.150
Don't do it!

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:42.910
Do what?!

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:46.760
There's a praying mantis here, 
so I was just going to grab it!

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:48.370
Huh? A praying mantis?

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.880
I wondered what was going on 
when you came charging at me.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.020
I couldn't help it!

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:57.220
I thought you were in despair 
because you got a zero.

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:59.050
Why would I hit the fire 
alarm out of despair?

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:24.900
Do all of our homework here?

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:29.620
So Nattsun and Hotarun and Koma-chan 
and Nii-nii are coming over, too.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:32.370
Okay. At 2:00.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:34.570
See you later.

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:40.380
Nee-nee, Koma-chan and everyone 
else is coming over.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.830
Nee-nee, wake up!

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.360
Huh?

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:51.150
What? What is it?

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:53.230
Koma-chan and everyone else is coming over.

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:55.730
We're all going to study together.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:57.690
Oh, that's right.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:01.170
I gave extra homework 
since it's a long break.

00:12:01.170 --> 00:12:03.250
You kids really work hard.

00:12:03.660 --> 00:12:07.610
Anyway, where's the TV remote?

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:10.080
Ren-chon, go get it.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:14.210
Huh? Wh-What's wrong?

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:18.310
Nee-nee, I don't think 
you should be like that.

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.830
Everyone's trying hard to get good grades.

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:26.750
So when our teacher acts 
sleepy while we take tests,

00:12:27.150 --> 00:12:29.610
and sleeps all day at home,

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:32.060
and won't even look for the remote,

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:35.850
Nattsun is never going to get motivated.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:40.890
I think it's a teacher's 
job to motivate everyone.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.780
Y-You're right...

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:48.590
I don't know about motivating everyone,

00:12:48.590 --> 00:12:50.490
but should I help you all study?

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:55.310
Yes. And use both praise and 
discipline to motivate us.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:57.010
That's easy for you to say...

00:12:57.010 --> 00:13:01.140
Then practice motivating me 
before the others get here!

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:02.090
Yeah!

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:04.470
Practice?

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:07.970
If I could do that in such a short 
time, I'd have a trouble-free life.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:13.290
Okay, okay. I'll do it.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:15.770
Okay, I'll pretend to study.

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:19.330
And you need to motivate me.

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:22.980
Uh... So is this like playing pretend?

00:13:22.980 --> 00:13:25.080
This is not playing pretend.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.700
It's real practice.

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:39.080
Oh, Ren-chon, you're studying? Good for you.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:40.500
Write, write.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.780
Is that Japanese you're working on?

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:43.650
That's right.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:46.880
The "wa" after your name is 
written with the hiragana "ha."

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:48.930
I'm doing math.

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.140
That's math?

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:53.170
Numbers come before and after the "wa."

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:54.770
I know!

00:13:55.140 --> 00:13:58.150
Why don't we do this like it's a video game?

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.420
A video game?

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.160
The questions are the enemies.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:03.230
You'll be the hero and defeat them.

00:14:03.640 --> 00:14:07.360
And with each one you defeat, a 
stronger enemy will come out.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:10.620
That sounds fun! I'm getting motivated!

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:13.680
Okay! Your first question is a slime!

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:15.500
Defeat it with your leaded sword!

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:18.420
Leaded sword?

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:20.420
You mean my pencil!

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:21.890
Stab!

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:26.200
Good! You defeated the slime and leveled up!

00:14:26.200 --> 00:14:28.380
I did it! I did it!

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:31.250
Nee-nee, next enemy! Next enemy!

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:33.090
Next enemy, huh?

00:14:33.090 --> 00:14:35.190
Um, the next enemy is...

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:39.650
Dun-da-da-dun! A dekopon has appeared!

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:41.610
What?! A dekopon?!

00:14:42.550 --> 00:14:45.840
Nee-nee, that's just a big tangerine.

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:49.850
Uh-oh, looks like this question 
might give you some trouble!

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:51.350
"Dekopon" refers to this.

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:51.370
It's a dekopon!

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:53.430
And the third question is...

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:57.120
...the one that summons the red 
pen: an Amaou strawberry!

00:14:57.120 --> 00:15:00.480
Oh, but the fourth is a Prince 
melon, so don't worry.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.580
You're doomed if the Yuubari 
melon shows up, though.

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:03.690
Nee-nee...

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:06.670
Oh! The fifth question is a dragonfruit!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.280
This one breathes fire! Uh-oh!

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.260
Nee-nee!

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:11.800
Huh? What's up?

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:13.900
This is weird.

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:16.430
I want to fight monsters.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:18.770
Why am I fighting fruit?

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:22.400
Well, to be honest, I don't 
know much about video games.

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:24.520
The slime was the only thing 
I could come up with.

00:15:24.810 --> 00:15:28.150
Nee-nee, why did you suggest 
making it a video game, then?

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:31.260
What other things appear in them?

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:37.950
Well, if you have a leaded sword 
equipped, you can beat a dragon.

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:41.590
Be sure to sharpen it and equip 
it, or there's no point.

00:15:42.110 --> 00:15:45.520
I'd rather eat fruits than fight them.

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:48.690
Okay, how about this?

00:15:48.690 --> 00:15:51.420
If you solve it, I'll reward you with cake.

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:52.890
What?! Cake?!

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:55.790
N-Nee-nee, when did you buy a cake?!

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:58.030
Is it shortcake? Chocolate cake?

00:15:58.030 --> 00:16:01.100
It doesn't matter what kind it 
is! I was just craving cake!

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:03.850
No, I didn't buy any.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:07.510
I just thought I'd say it and 
see if it motivated you.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.860
So, what were we doing?

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:15.060
Oh, right! Do you think 
you can beat the dekopon?

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:20.060
The dekopon is two-digit subtraction, 
so maybe it's too hard.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:22.030
...it.

00:16:22.030 --> 00:16:24.080
Huh? What'd you say?

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:25.500
Forget it.

00:16:26.070 --> 00:16:28.820
I've had enough of this game of pretend.

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:31.440
My heart just got subtracted.

00:16:31.440 --> 00:16:34.550
Whoa... Ren-chon, you're 
too unmotivated now...

00:16:36.500 --> 00:16:38.910
I know. Instead of the way you teach,

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:41.010
why don't you straighten up the way you look?

00:16:41.010 --> 00:16:44.150
A teacher who looks reliable 
would motivate us.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.210
Like how?

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:48.520
Sit up straighter.

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:53.660
And I think you should 
wear a suit to school.

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:55.900
And also...

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:07.170
Oh! A dekopon!

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:10.490
A dekopon! A dekopon! Can you solve it?

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:11.800
We're done with that!

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:14.550
You're sleeping more than usual today!

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:17.160
I'm telling you that you should shape up!

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:18.970
Oh, sorry, sorry.

00:17:18.970 --> 00:17:24.050
See, I was actually up late 
last night making handouts,

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:25.980
so I didn't get much sleep.

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:28.010
You were working at night?

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:31.940
But I didn't see you doing 
any work last night.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:36.450
I worked late, after you went to bed.

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:38.040
Oh...

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:40.890
S-So that's why.

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:44.120
I didn't know, and I made you wake up.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.640
I'm sorry.

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:49.210
Hey, I don't mind.

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:53.670
But after you told me all that, 
I'll just have to do my best.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:54.920
Okay!

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:57.930
I'm going to sleep now and 
preserve my strength!

00:17:57.930 --> 00:17:59.890
If you have any trouble studying,

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:02.180
just smack me awake anytime.

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:04.430
B-But, Nee-nee...

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:06.840
Don't worry, Ren-chon!

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:11.260
Just watch me help everyone 
study and motivate them!

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:13.350
Not that.

00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:17.190
If you sleep here, you'll be in the way.

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:21.200
Oh. Right.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.790
You'll be studying in this room...

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:24.870
Okay, okay.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.640
You're still not motivated, are you?

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:29.820
You should sleep in your futon.

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:32.700
Okay, then take me to my futon.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:35.710
What are you talking about? 
At least do that much yourself.

00:18:36.050 --> 00:18:38.170
Aww, come on.

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:40.180
It's a pain to take off my mask.

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:43.660
It's a pain to take off your 
mask? It's just for a minute!

00:18:43.660 --> 00:18:46.250
Aww, don't say that.

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:48.520
C'mon, c'mon...

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:51.980
Please, Ren-chon!

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:55.810
C'mon! Just to my futon!

00:18:53.520 --> 00:18:55.890
<i>I guess there's really no hope for Nee-nee.</i>

00:18:55.810 --> 00:19:02.160
Please!

00:18:57.120 --> 00:18:58.970
<i>In that case, I'll...</i>

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:02.160
<i>I'll have to motivate everyone!</i>

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:04.120
Okay, fine.

00:19:04.330 --> 00:19:06.810
But shape up starting tomorrow, okay?

00:19:06.810 --> 00:19:08.060
Sure.

00:19:11.220 --> 00:19:13.540
Wait here for a second.

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:15.080
Okay.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:27.390
Nee-nee, there are slippers 
in front of you. Put them on.

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:31.050
Oh, there...

00:19:32.530 --> 00:19:35.220
Now spin around.

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:41.110
But now I won't know which way is which...

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:43.270
It's no fun if you do it the normal way.

00:19:43.270 --> 00:19:47.040
Oh, I get it. Like breaking 
a watermelon, huh?

00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:50.370
Now just go straight.

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:54.200
Careful. There's a step there.

00:19:54.200 --> 00:19:57.590
Is there a step in our hallway?

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:00.500
Keep going straight.

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:02.340
Okay.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:10.480
Man, why do we have to study over a break?

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:12.680
Let's just lay around at home.

00:20:12.680 --> 00:20:13.810
Sheesh...

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:18.070
If you laze around and your grades 
drop, Mom will get mad again.

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:23.240
But Kazu-nee is lazy, and she's 
a proper working grown-up.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:27.530
I think things would work out 
even if I didn't try too hard.

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:29.500
Huh?

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:35.220
Ren-chon, is this it?

00:20:36.810 --> 00:20:40.170
It's so dark. I'll take a spill 
before I see my pillow.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:43.840
Spill-o before my pillow! 
Oh, man, I crack me up!

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:49.260
Hey, Ren-chon, did you hear that? 
A spill-o before my pillow!

00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:54.040
Uh, Ren-chon? Are you over here?

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:58.230
Oh, Ren-chon! Gotcha!

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:03.730
Ren-chon, did you hear what I 
said? A spill-o before my pillow!

00:21:01.920 --> 00:21:04.890
Nee-chan, I'll try harder.

00:21:05.310 --> 00:21:07.160
Huh? Ren-chon, you feel kinda—

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:06.460
Yeah.

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:18.420
Ren-chon! Where's my pillow?

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:26.010
Koshigaya Natsumi

00:21:28.510 --> 00:21:31.970
All right! I got a 75!

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:34.150
Studying together was worth it.

00:21:34.150 --> 00:21:36.400
You got a good grade on your make-up test.

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:37.440
Thanks!

00:21:37.440 --> 00:21:41.400
Yeah, you know, if you work 
hard, it shows in your results.

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:44.650
That sounds totally different 
from everything you said before.

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:47.210
I got a 100 again!

00:21:49.170 --> 00:21:53.830
There's nothing but curry 
in this red bean bun...

00:21:54.240 --> 00:21:58.340
No, look. This is kheema curry.

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:02.360
It's gotta at least have red beans in it.

00:22:02.360 --> 00:22:06.010
The collaboration of sweet 
and spicy is important—

00:22:10.410 --> 00:22:16.460
<b>Non Non Biyori</b>

00:22:16.460 --> 00:22:21.550
<b>That's all for today</b>

00:23:41.150 --> 00:23:43.850
<i>Frogs are grown-ups,</i>

00:23:43.850 --> 00:23:46.930
<i>tadpoles are children.</i>

00:23:46.930 --> 00:23:50.160
<i>When they grow hind legs, they're moochers.</i>

00:23:50.160 --> 00:23:53.490
<i>When they grow front legs, 
they're in a rebellious stage.</i>

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.490
<b>Episode 4</b>

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:53.490
<b>I Made a Teru-teru Bouzu</b>

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:55.990
<b>Non Non Biyori
Repeat</b>

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:55.990
Photo: To-a

00:23:53.490 --> 00:23:55.990
Please Watch Again
